    <briefdescription>
<para>In-memory implementation of <ref refid="classthemis_1_1projects_1_1_i_project_audit_log" kindref="compound">IProjectAuditLog</ref>. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Thread-safe append-only log intended for:<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>unit/integration testing without storage dependencies</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>in-process audit trail (bounded to <computeroutput>max_entries</computeroutput>)</para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
<para>Production deployments should use a persistent sink (e.g. RocksDB or an append-only event store). This implementation is a production-quality in-process sink: bounded capacity, thread-safe, and compliant with <ref refid="classthemis_1_1projects_1_1_i_project_audit_log" kindref="compound">IProjectAuditLog</ref>.</para>
<para>Capacity and eviction ───────────────────── When the log reaches <computeroutput>max_entries</computeroutput>, the oldest 10 % of entries are dropped to keep memory bounded. Default capacity is 100 000 entries. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
